  {
   "kind": "paragraph",
   "text": "## Cubes"
  },
  {
   "kind": "paragraph",
   "text": "To cube a number we multiply the number by itself, and then multiply that answer by the number again."
  },
  {
   "kind": "paragraph",
   "text": "We can write cubed using a small (superscript) 3.  \n2³ means 2 cubed  \n3³ means 3 cubed"
  },
  {
   "kind": "worked-example",
   "title": "Example 3: Work out the value of 4³",
   "steps": [
    {
     "heading": null,
     "body": "To work out the value of 4 cubed we need to calculate 4 × 4 × 4  \n4 × 4 = 16  \n16 × 4 = 64  \n4³ = 64",
     "figure_refs": []
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "kind": "worked-example",
   "title": "Example 4: Work out the value of 10³",
   "steps": [
    {
     "heading": null,
     "body": "To work out the value of 10 cubed we need to calculate 10 × 10 × 10  \n10 × 10 = 100  \n100 × 10 = 1000  \n10³ = 1000",
     "figure_refs": []
    }
   ]
  },
  {
