  {
   "kind": "paragraph",
   "text": "## Square Roots"
  },
  {
   "kind": "paragraph",
   "text": "Square rooting is the opposite of sqauring a number.  \n9² = 81, so the square root of 81 is 9"
  },
  {
   "kind": "paragraph",
   "text": "Square root 100 can be written as √100  \n√81 means square root 81"
  },
  {
   "kind": "worked-example",
   "title": "Example 5: Work out the value of √144",
   "steps": [
    {
     "heading": null,
     "body": "We are looking for the number that multiplies by itself to make 144  \n12 × 12 = 144  \n√144 = 12",
     "figure_refs": []
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "kind": "worked-example",
   "title": "Example 6: Work out the value of √100",
   "steps": [
    {
     "heading": null,
     "body": "We are looking for the number that multiplies by itself to make 100  \n10 × 10 = 100  \n√100 = 10",
     "figure_refs": []
    }
   ]
  },
  {
