  {
   "kind": "paragraph",
   "text": "## Cube Roots"
  },
  {
   "kind": "paragraph",
   "text": "Cube rooting is the opposite of cubing a number.  \n10³ = 1000, so the cube root of 1000 is 10"
  },
  {
   "kind": "paragraph",
   "text": "Cube root 125 can be written as ∛125  \n∛216 means cube root 216"
  },
  {
   "kind": "worked-example",
   "title": "Example 7: Work out the value of ∛8",
   "steps": [
    {
     "heading": null,
     "body": "We are looking for the number that multiplies by itself, and then by itself again, to make 8  \n2 × 2 × 2 = 8  \n∛8 = 2",
     "figure_refs": []
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "kind": "mcq-set",
   "items": [
    {
     "id": "a2813695-1721-436d-b37e-3f4b01c93951",
     "prompt": "Find $\\sqrt[3]{343}$.",
