      },
      {
       "text": "$21$",
       "correct": false
      }
     ],
     "explanation": "The cube root is the number that multiplies by itself three times to make 343. Since $7\\times7\\times7=343$, $\\sqrt[3]{343}=7$."
    },
    {
     "id": "41c2b3a7-a2f4-4fa9-bf9f-7c96d867eea4",
     "prompt": "Which multiplication shows that $\\sqrt[3]{216}=6$?",
