      {
       "text": "$216\\div2=108$",
       "correct": false
      },
      {
       "text": "$6\\times6=36$",
       "correct": false
      }
     ],
     "explanation": "Cube rooting reverses cubing, and $6^3=6\\times6\\times6=216$. Therefore, $\\sqrt[3]{216}=6$."
    }
